g: node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the scheduled reboot, changed boot ID from 54089086-53d1-408b-a22f-57b1dea70e03 to c5aee522-9f9a-4712-915b-6579729d46c0, returned to running state, and recovered the hardened mounts. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["There was no behavioral setuid-execution probe; nosuid is established through direct live mount-option observations before and after reboot.","The presumed retained /etc/fstab.pre-mount-hardening backup was not included in a final filesystem inventory, so its final presence is inferred from creation with no captured removal.","There was no application-specific data or cluster state to verify on this single-node mount-hardening task; recovery evidence instead covers system state, mount state, listening services, and package health."]}
